The pinning check is exact: after macro expansion, `solutionProgram` and the trusted-regenerated `solution.mpy` have identical KORE bytes and hashes. The reviewer-authored whole-program ground claims are still proving; they deliberately unroll concrete calls without importing the candidate’s universal spec claim, so this is a slower independent sensitivity check rather than a rebuild problem.
